# Voicememo vocabulary

User-specific terms the speech model gets wrong. The transcribe script reads
every non-empty, non-heading line from this file and passes them to the
OpenAI transcription API as the `prompt` hint — a vocabulary bias for
decoding.

How to edit:
- Add a word per line, or a few comma-separated. Both work.
- Group however you like under `##` headings — they're skipped at parse time.
- Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
- The whole file is one bag of words — order and section names don't reach the API.

What belongs here:
- Names of family, friends, colleagues you mention by name.
- Niche brands/platforms the model probably doesn't know (local startups,
  internal tools, regional services).
- Your project codenames.
- Local street, neighborhood, or venue names that get mangled in your area.

What does NOT belong:
- Global brands (Sony, Audi, Tesla, ChatGPT, Twitter) — already known.
- Major cities or countries — already known.
- Generic English jargon (API, AI, podcast) — already known.
- Famous public figures — already known.

The prompt has a ~200-word effective ceiling, so every general term you
add displaces a genuinely useful one. Keep it tight.

After editing, future recordings pick up the new vocab automatically. To
re-transcribe existing memos with the new vocab, delete their cached
transcript: `rm ~/Documents/Sony/.cache/transcripts/<basename>.txt`.

---

## Family
<!-- e.g Andreas, Микола, Васо -->

## People
<!-- Friends, colleagues, regular collaborators. -->

## Local brands and platforms
<!-- e.g. DOU, Djinni — services well-known in your region but not globally. -->

## Project codenames
<!-- Internal product or feature names you talk about. -->

## Local places
<!-- Street / neighborhood / venue names the model mishears. -->
